            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.11.1</h2>
<p><b>Task finder reliability.</b> A small fix so Jarvis still finds your tasks
when its preferred model isn't available to your API key, and tells you clearly
when it genuinely can't reach the model.</p>
<ul>
  <li>If Jarvis's task finder can't use its preferred model with your key, it now
      automatically falls back to another available model instead of quietly
      showing an empty day.</li>
  <li>When the finder truly can't reach the model, it now says so — "Couldn't
      reach the model. Check your API key and its model access." — instead of the
      misleading "Could not decide."</li>
  <li>No changes to your data, your Slack connection, or what leaves your Mac.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
